WEBVTT

00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:11.820
Kaito, let's do a puzzle.

00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:14.380
What is it?

00:00:15.220 --> 00:00:17.260
Weren't you going to save me?

00:00:20.310 --> 00:00:22.490
I can see it, Kaito...

00:00:23.410 --> 00:00:25.240
Our puzzle time!

00:00:31.890 --> 00:00:33.020
Why?

00:00:33.890 --> 00:00:38.010
Why did Nonoha Itou appear in my and Kaito's future?

00:01:08.330 --> 00:01:10.000
Lost

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:13.130
Tesaguri de sagashiteta
I've searched, groping

00:01:14.920 --> 00:01:17.050
Tozasareta mirai no kotae nante doko nimo nai
The answer to a future that's been closed off

00:01:17.050 --> 00:01:18.970
Tozasareta mirai no kotae nante doko nimo nai
Is nowhere to be found

00:01:18.970 --> 00:01:22.310
Hashiru shoudou, ima kaidoku funou
The impulse to run, it's impossible to decipher now

00:01:22.310 --> 00:01:24.020
Found

00:01:24.020 --> 00:01:28.270
Kudaketa hazu no unmei o
A fate that was supposedly smashed

00:01:28.270 --> 00:01:32.730
Mijuku na yume no naka de kikoeta kitanda
I've come to hear it within that half-formed dream:

00:01:32.730 --> 00:01:35.570
Saigo made I'll be there for you
Until the end, I'll be there for you

00:01:35.570 --> 00:01:38.660
Tachidomaranai, kono hari dake wa
It won't stop, not this needle

00:01:38.660 --> 00:01:41.990
Boku no asu o kizamu oto o tsukisasu
It will pierce the sound that engraves my tomorrow

00:01:41.990 --> 00:01:43.910
Shinjitsu kara nigetara ima
If I run from the truth, then now...

00:01:43.910 --> 00:01:45.620
Genjitsu ni mo maketara ima
If I lose to reality, then now...

00:01:45.620 --> 00:01:47.960
Nani ga nokoru no?
What will remain?

00:01:47.960 --> 00:01:50.170
(Nokoru no?)
(Will remain?)

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:52.540
Kazoekirenai kono kizu dake ga
These countless wounds of mine

00:01:52.540 --> 00:01:56.010
Boku no kinou o zanzou to shite kataru
They tell of my yesterday as an afterimage

00:01:56.010 --> 00:01:57.720
Unmei ga hodoketemo ima
Even if fate were unraveled, now...

00:01:57.720 --> 00:01:59.550
Sonzai o kowashitemo ima
Even if my existence were smashed, now...

00:01:59.550 --> 00:02:02.430
Boku no michi o yuku yo
I will travel my path

00:02:02.970 --> 00:02:04.560
It's now or never

00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:05.640
That is what they say

00:02:05.640 --> 00:02:07.730
Live your life today, yeah, yeah

00:02:07.730 --> 00:02:11.400
There will always be,
there will always be a way

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:12.560
That is what they say

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:14.730
Live your life today, yeah, yeah

00:02:14.730 --> 00:02:18.240
There will always be,
there will always be a way

00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:19.450
That is what they say

00:02:19.450 --> 00:02:21.870
Live your life today, yeah, yeah

00:02:24.040 --> 00:02:28.000
The Closed-Off World

00:02:28.640 --> 00:02:31.050
He really said that, right?

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:34.200
Yeah, he gave Pinochle a message that

00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:35.970
he's waiting at the Puzzle of God.

00:02:37.720 --> 00:02:39.720
I'm friggin' shocked.

00:02:39.720 --> 00:02:42.550
I never thought the Puzzle of God would come up now.

00:02:43.350 --> 00:02:48.180
Count Pythagoras and Jin
fought at the Puzzle of God, right?

00:02:48.520 --> 00:02:52.930
Yes, but it collapsed after their battle.

00:02:53.540 --> 00:02:57.940
The POG is currently unable to confirm
if there is another one.

00:02:58.640 --> 00:03:00.450
Then, what are we supposed to do?

00:03:01.170 --> 00:03:03.000
The Puzzle of God is

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:05.440
a puzzle that cannot be solved unless two

00:03:05.440 --> 00:03:07.170
Phi-Brains wage their lives.

00:03:08.540 --> 00:03:11.130
But I ain't a Phi-Brain.

00:03:11.130 --> 00:03:12.180
Not now.

00:03:13.420 --> 00:03:18.260
Why did Freecell take the Final Ring from Klondike?

00:03:18.930 --> 00:03:23.760
He already had a Ring equal to the real thing.

00:03:24.850 --> 00:03:27.090
The only conceivable reason is...

00:03:30.270 --> 00:03:31.210
Kaito?

00:03:31.650 --> 00:03:36.500
Rook, can the POG help
and find out where Freecell is?

00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:38.190
You're going, aren't you?

00:03:39.110 --> 00:03:39.820
Yeah.

00:03:40.450 --> 00:03:42.250
Even though that guy's a monster?

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:46.700
Klondike beat you, but this son of a
bitch is even more powerful!

00:03:48.120 --> 00:03:49.610
I made a promise.

00:03:50.460 --> 00:03:54.780
I'll fulfill the promise to begin puzzle time with Freecell.

00:03:55.710 --> 00:03:57.540
And I'll rescue him!

00:04:04.390 --> 00:04:07.720
To think this is how Klondike's ambitions
would be thwarted...

00:04:08.100 --> 00:04:09.970
I couldn't have imagined it.

00:04:10.490 --> 00:04:13.090
I'm grateful for your help.

00:04:14.230 --> 00:04:15.480
Let's go back.

00:04:15.480 --> 00:04:17.010
We could use a little rest.

00:04:17.780 --> 00:04:19.020
Thank you.

00:04:20.200 --> 00:04:21.610
What is it, Pinochle?

00:04:25.040 --> 00:04:26.200
Freecell, huh?

00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:30.410
To me, Freecell's running wild...

00:04:30.920 --> 00:04:32.960
sounded like cries.

00:04:34.960 --> 00:04:36.240
It was sad.

00:04:47.270 --> 00:04:48.060
Kaito!

00:04:50.350 --> 00:04:50.970
Freecell!

00:04:51.850 --> 00:04:54.730
Kaito, let's do a puzzle.

00:04:56.650 --> 00:04:57.780
What is it?

00:04:58.440 --> 00:05:00.610
Weren't you going to save me?

00:05:03.530 --> 00:05:05.590
I can see it, Kaito.

00:05:06.410 --> 00:05:08.310
Our puzzle time!

00:05:17.130 --> 00:05:18.310
A dream...

00:05:19.170 --> 00:05:20.350
The future again.

00:05:22.220 --> 00:05:23.620
What time is it?

00:05:30.310 --> 00:05:31.060
What's this?!

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:37.310
Freecell, what are you thinking?!

00:05:38.940 --> 00:05:40.900
Miss Nonoha Itou is...

00:05:40.900 --> 00:05:43.070
She is with us.

00:05:43.820 --> 00:05:45.530
She and Mr. Freecell await

00:05:45.530 --> 00:05:51.000
Kaito Daimon's arrival at the Puzzle of God.

00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:52.020
The location is...

00:05:53.370 --> 00:05:55.460
Sure enough, there's a strange, giant structure

00:05:55.460 --> 00:05:57.560
at the specified coordinates.

00:05:58.050 --> 00:06:01.130
It's probably owned by the Loewenherz Foundation.

00:06:02.380 --> 00:06:05.380
I'm reading the transmitter
placed on Nonoha at that location!

00:06:05.930 --> 00:06:07.820
Looks like it's for real then.

00:06:08.470 --> 00:06:11.810
Kaito, we still don't know what our enemy is after.

00:06:12.310 --> 00:06:14.560
We'll do a little research on our end,

00:06:14.560 --> 00:06:15.780
but keep your guard up.

00:06:16.270 --> 00:06:17.410
Yeah, I know.

00:06:17.950 --> 00:06:18.980
Thank you.

00:06:23.650 --> 00:06:26.220
Pullin' a dirty trick like takin' a hostage...

00:06:26.620 --> 00:06:28.650
If somethin' happens to Nonoha, they've had it!

00:06:29.150 --> 00:06:31.360
Kaito would have kept his promise

00:06:31.360 --> 00:06:33.440
without them taking a hostage.

00:06:34.010 --> 00:06:35.370
He doesn't get it, huh?

00:06:36.120 --> 00:06:38.370
That bothers me too.

00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:41.880
Is Nonoha just a hostage?

00:06:42.380 --> 00:06:44.350
Huh? Meaning what?

00:06:44.970 --> 00:06:47.010
I don't know yet.

00:06:47.850 --> 00:06:51.800
In any case, we won't know till we see Freecell.

00:07:03.940 --> 00:07:04.820
Please.

00:07:06.700 --> 00:07:08.690
Don't you "Please" me! There's no "Please"!

00:07:09.120 --> 00:07:11.080
Meaning?

00:07:11.080 --> 00:07:14.700
I came here 'cuz he said he wanted to talk to me.

00:07:15.000 --> 00:07:16.290
What is this place?!

00:07:16.290 --> 00:07:18.000
Where am I?!

00:07:18.000 --> 00:07:19.710
The Himalayan mountain range.

00:07:20.400 --> 00:07:22.540
Th..The Himalayas?!

00:07:23.840 --> 00:07:25.540
The Himalayas.

00:07:26.180 --> 00:07:28.270
I don't believe it!

00:07:28.270 --> 00:07:30.050
A "talk" in the Himalayas?

00:07:30.850 --> 00:07:35.050
I thought it was strange how we stayed on that plane!

00:07:31.640 --> 00:07:35.050
You've complicated things, Whist.

00:07:35.180 --> 00:07:35.890
The Himalayas...

00:07:35.890 --> 00:07:37.640
My apologies,
The Himalayas...

00:07:37.640 --> 00:07:41.830
but it was necessary for the game to begin.

00:07:42.440 --> 00:07:43.690
Well, fine.

00:07:45.030 --> 00:07:49.360
I am a little curious about that girl.

00:07:50.070 --> 00:07:52.860
And? What's your evil plan this time?

00:07:54.540 --> 00:07:56.540
Don't be so uptight.

00:07:56.540 --> 00:07:59.020
Whist makes a superb cup of tea.

00:07:59.750 --> 00:08:01.620
Drink before it gets cold.

00:08:04.210 --> 00:08:08.090
It's been a while,
since you and I helped Kaito together.

00:08:08.090 --> 00:08:09.800
Wow, it's great!

00:08:09.800 --> 00:08:12.510
Ah, um, yes.

00:08:12.970 --> 00:08:14.560
I saw the future.

00:08:15.390 --> 00:08:18.840
And in it, you were there as well as Kaito.

00:08:19.820 --> 00:08:20.890
I wonder why?

00:08:22.780 --> 00:08:25.310
There's no way I could know that.

00:08:25.730 --> 00:08:29.360
But I do know that you don't understand Kaito at all.

00:08:30.240 --> 00:08:31.820
I don't understand?

00:08:32.320 --> 00:08:33.530
That's right.

00:08:33.530 --> 00:08:35.330
Kaito would have kept his promise

00:08:35.330 --> 00:08:37.160
without you taking a hostage.

00:08:37.620 --> 00:08:39.630
Kaito, keep his promise?

00:08:40.710 --> 00:08:43.000
That's of no consequence.

00:08:43.790 --> 00:08:46.420
His coming here was a future already written.

00:08:47.840 --> 00:08:49.590
It's not of no consequence!

00:08:49.590 --> 00:08:51.260
Kaito said as much.

00:08:52.050 --> 00:08:53.670
That he'd keep his promise.

00:08:56.270 --> 00:08:57.890
Really?

00:08:57.890 --> 00:08:58.930
Really?!

00:08:59.770 --> 00:09:01.490
Kaito said that?

00:09:03.190 --> 00:09:07.060
I see, the promise Kaito made to me...

00:09:12.200 --> 00:09:13.620
What's with you?

00:09:13.620 --> 00:09:16.650
Wasn't Kaito's promise "of no consequence"?

00:09:18.700 --> 00:09:19.950
Oh, that's right.

00:09:21.290 --> 00:09:22.400
Now's a good time.

00:09:24.880 --> 00:09:25.990
Here's this back.

00:09:26.740 --> 00:09:29.980
Sure enough, you should have
your mother's memento.

00:09:32.590 --> 00:09:33.770
There you go.

00:09:35.350 --> 00:09:38.820
Again, you've made me remember something

00:09:38.820 --> 00:09:40.000
I don't want to remember.

00:09:41.850 --> 00:09:42.850
That day...

00:10:01.710 --> 00:10:03.120
Nonoha...

00:10:03.120 --> 00:10:04.300
Be safe!

00:10:06.130 --> 00:10:08.920
This is a puzzle,

00:10:09.760 --> 00:10:12.380
but I just can't solve it.

00:10:15.800 --> 00:10:16.630
It's strange.

00:10:17.260 --> 00:10:19.640
Even now, I can't solve it.

00:10:24.600 --> 00:10:29.450
This is the puzzle I wanted Kaito to solve with me.

00:10:31.860 --> 00:10:35.990
I wanted to solve this puzzle
to make my mama happy.

00:10:38.660 --> 00:10:41.660
But now, I just don't care.

00:10:42.540 --> 00:10:43.580
Not about the promise,

00:10:45.080 --> 00:10:46.080
or about Mama.

00:10:47.750 --> 00:10:48.830
Solitia...

00:10:51.170 --> 00:10:52.580
That's your mama, right?

00:10:54.170 --> 00:10:56.210
How do you know Mama's name?

00:10:57.220 --> 00:11:00.680
Solitia was your mama.

00:11:02.640 --> 00:11:05.470
She was the first victim of the Replica Ring.

00:11:22.080 --> 00:11:24.990
"I am in the midst of anguish."

00:11:25.830 --> 00:11:28.710
"Happiness fairly brimming with light,"

00:11:28.710 --> 00:11:31.180
"and malice as if blown from the depths of the earth..."

00:11:32.590 --> 00:11:34.960
"I am buffeted by a wave of emotions

00:11:34.960 --> 00:11:37.250
that drives me between the two."

00:11:39.010 --> 00:11:41.180
"I love Freecell,"

00:11:41.180 --> 00:11:43.960
"and yet in the next moment I find myself loathing him."

00:11:45.520 --> 00:11:49.840
"Why am I unable to smile at him?"

00:11:55.190 --> 00:11:58.480
That was written in a diary found in your old house.

00:12:00.030 --> 00:12:01.540
It's the truth.

00:12:02.790 --> 00:12:05.530
Her mind had been twisted by the Ring.

00:12:06.210 --> 00:12:09.920
Your mama suffered, caught between good and evil.

00:12:12.340 --> 00:12:13.920
You knew, didn't you?

00:12:13.920 --> 00:12:16.340
That your mama loved you?

00:12:17.800 --> 00:12:18.710
Huh...

00:12:20.720 --> 00:12:22.510
Wait, that's all?!

00:12:22.510 --> 00:12:24.520
This is the shocking truth!

00:12:24.520 --> 00:12:26.470
Can't you be a little happier?

00:12:27.180 --> 00:12:29.270
Say what you will,

00:12:29.270 --> 00:12:31.730
but I hated my mama.

00:12:31.730 --> 00:12:32.480
Knowing her past changes nothing.

00:12:33.730 --> 00:12:36.820
Listen here, the truth is, your mama was kind.

00:12:36.820 --> 00:12:38.320
The Ring was evil!

00:12:38.320 --> 00:12:40.030
You're amazing.

00:12:40.030 --> 00:12:41.040
Huh?

00:12:41.740 --> 00:12:43.670
You can memorize a whole diary

00:12:43.670 --> 00:12:45.700
after reading it just once, right?

00:12:47.750 --> 00:12:52.050
Say, what else was written in Mama's diary?

00:12:55.550 --> 00:12:56.550
Understood.

00:12:57.760 --> 00:12:59.990
No matter, please open the gate.

00:13:00.840 --> 00:13:01.420
Um...

00:13:02.340 --> 00:13:03.170
Yes?

00:13:03.600 --> 00:13:07.180
Sorry, could I have a pen and some paper?

00:13:27.830 --> 00:13:29.160
Okay, here.

00:13:31.890 --> 00:13:35.500
It's the puzzle my mama
made for me when I was little.

00:13:38.170 --> 00:13:39.750
This takes me back...

00:13:43.930 --> 00:13:46.480
Ah, this goes here.

00:13:49.270 --> 00:13:51.480
What's with that smile?

00:13:51.480 --> 00:13:54.270
This puzzle was made by the mom
he supposedly hates.

00:13:59.320 --> 00:14:01.270
It's an installation on a massive scale.

00:14:02.030 --> 00:14:05.530
It's probably a secret Foundation
laboratory or something.

00:14:06.450 --> 00:14:08.700
And you're getting Nonoha's signal?

00:14:08.700 --> 00:14:11.530
Yes, we're getting close to the transmitter.

00:14:12.370 --> 00:14:15.040
They're bein' eerily nice, huh?

00:14:16.540 --> 00:14:18.840
He loves and yet hates his mom.

00:14:19.340 --> 00:14:21.970
He doesn't care about Kaito's promise,

00:14:21.970 --> 00:14:24.060
yet he's happy he kept it.

00:14:26.300 --> 00:14:28.340
Two conflicting emotions...

00:14:28.930 --> 00:14:32.490
Bound by them, he's made this closed-off world.

00:14:33.350 --> 00:14:35.560
It's gotten so he can't get out of here.

00:14:37.270 --> 00:14:39.310
This is the Orpheus Ring's fault.

00:14:39.780 --> 00:14:42.370
Freecell, let's take the Ring off!

00:14:43.150 --> 00:14:45.570
You can't keep that Ring off any longer!

00:14:45.990 --> 00:14:47.030
I solved it!

00:14:47.030 --> 00:14:48.280
Don't you get it?

00:14:48.280 --> 00:14:52.070
Your mama suffered between two sentiments too!

00:14:52.540 --> 00:14:54.330
Huh? What?

00:14:55.750 --> 00:14:57.300
I never noticed...

00:14:58.040 --> 00:15:01.090
This puzzle has another answer.

00:15:02.590 --> 00:15:05.520
If you line up letters with the same numbers...

00:15:08.720 --> 00:15:11.350
"You are my hope."

00:15:17.810 --> 00:15:20.100
Hey, what...

00:15:26.700 --> 00:15:27.740
Your hair...

00:15:28.280 --> 00:15:29.610
Would you put it down?

00:15:31.910 --> 00:15:33.360
What gives, all of a sudden?

00:15:34.000 --> 00:15:35.370
Please!

00:15:44.340 --> 00:15:46.410
You look just like her.

00:15:47.430 --> 00:15:49.160
You have Mama's pendant,

00:15:49.890 --> 00:15:51.880
you've memorized her diary...

00:15:53.020 --> 00:15:55.820
You know things about my mama even I didn't.

00:15:58.230 --> 00:15:59.980
You are...

00:15:59.980 --> 00:16:01.390
my mama!

00:16:07.950 --> 00:16:10.070
Just watch, Mama.

00:16:10.070 --> 00:16:13.410
My puzzle time with Kaito will start soon.

00:16:14.620 --> 00:16:17.170
Kaito is my eternal aspiration.

00:16:17.920 --> 00:16:20.410
I will become Kaito.

00:16:24.340 --> 00:16:25.510
What was that?

00:16:25.510 --> 00:16:27.170
Kaito's gone to see Freecell?

00:16:27.930 --> 00:16:29.470
Understood.

00:16:29.470 --> 00:16:30.760
Is that for real?

00:16:30.760 --> 00:16:31.920
Looks like it.

00:16:32.300 --> 00:16:33.510
Please!

00:16:33.510 --> 00:16:34.930
Let's go there too.

00:16:35.720 --> 00:16:36.930
I intend to.

00:16:45.150 --> 00:16:47.190
This is a big place.

00:16:47.700 --> 00:16:50.160
Freecell and Nonoha are here?

00:16:50.160 --> 00:16:51.840
They should be.

00:16:53.950 --> 00:16:55.740
My apologies for the wait.

00:16:55.740 --> 00:16:56.660
Whist!

00:16:56.660 --> 00:16:57.830
Bastard!
Whist!

00:16:57.830 --> 00:16:58.960
Where is Nonoha?

00:16:58.960 --> 00:17:00.330
Give her back right now!

00:17:01.130 --> 00:17:02.460
Mr. Kaito Daimon...

00:17:03.170 --> 00:17:06.390
I have observed many of your exploits up to today,

00:17:06.390 --> 00:17:08.130
and have firm conviction...

00:17:09.340 --> 00:17:13.130
You can fight Freecell as an equal.

00:17:13.760 --> 00:17:16.890
Whist, just who are you?

00:17:17.520 --> 00:17:19.960
One who wishes the great cause of

00:17:19.960 --> 00:17:23.000
the Orpheus Order to become manifest...

00:17:23.810 --> 00:17:25.390
As did Solitia.

00:17:26.980 --> 00:17:29.240
That's Freecell's mother's name!

00:17:29.650 --> 00:17:30.440
How do you...

00:17:31.280 --> 00:17:33.070
Both she and I

00:17:33.070 --> 00:17:35.050
wished for the birth of the Great One

00:17:35.050 --> 00:17:37.240
who will lead humanity to nirvana.

00:17:38.080 --> 00:17:40.950
Klondike was little more than a tool to that end.

00:17:41.420 --> 00:17:43.450
You want to make God, is that it?

00:17:43.880 --> 00:17:47.460
No, man shall surpass God!

00:17:48.260 --> 00:17:51.210
He who wins this fight will be
the one to free humanity,

00:17:51.590 --> 00:17:56.010
the true owner of the Orpheus Ring!

00:17:56.810 --> 00:17:58.930
Now then, let's begin...

00:17:58.930 --> 00:18:01.770
This ceremony to give birth to the Great One!

00:18:10.400 --> 00:18:11.320
Nonoha!

00:18:11.860 --> 00:18:12.980
Kaito!

00:18:13.740 --> 00:18:15.450
Everyone!

00:18:15.450 --> 00:18:17.080
You're okay?

00:18:17.080 --> 00:18:18.160
No injuries?

00:18:18.160 --> 00:18:20.040
No, I'm fine.

00:18:20.550 --> 00:18:21.830
Thank you for coming.

00:18:21.830 --> 00:18:25.250
Th..That guy d..didn't do nothin' to ya?

00:18:25.250 --> 00:18:27.180
Um, not especially.

00:18:27.630 --> 00:18:30.590
We drank tea and did a puzzle together.

00:18:30.590 --> 00:18:31.590
A puzzle?

00:18:32.050 --> 00:18:35.090
Yes, a puzzle that Solitia made.

00:18:35.550 --> 00:18:38.600
Then he called me his mama and stuff.

00:18:41.100 --> 00:18:43.520
Well, it's about time for you to disappear...

00:18:44.440 --> 00:18:45.100
Whist.

00:18:46.900 --> 00:18:50.070
There was no sign of you in the future I saw.

00:18:50.070 --> 00:18:52.610
Probably not in the future Kaito saw either.

00:18:54.200 --> 00:18:55.360
Mr. Freecell...

00:18:55.950 --> 00:19:01.120
I am to serve either you or Kaito Daimon,
whomever is victor.

00:19:01.120 --> 00:19:02.740
You're a pain.

00:19:03.660 --> 00:19:07.300
I don't want your eyes sullying

00:19:08.000 --> 00:19:10.590
the final, sacred game that Kaito and I play.

00:19:10.590 --> 00:19:11.500
But...

00:19:13.220 --> 00:19:14.500
Begone!

00:19:29.690 --> 00:19:33.270
Kaito, you wish to save me?

00:19:34.320 --> 00:19:35.820
Then save me.

00:19:35.820 --> 00:19:38.780
Win the game and take off the Ring.

00:19:41.540 --> 00:19:42.830
Hey, what the?!

00:19:42.830 --> 00:19:45.030
Unfortunately,

00:19:45.330 --> 00:19:47.540
you can't win as you are now.

00:19:48.500 --> 00:19:51.040
Want to try coming up to my level?

00:19:53.420 --> 00:19:54.370
Kaito!

00:20:06.560 --> 00:20:08.780
It's hopeless if you're not here with me.

00:20:15.820 --> 00:20:16.860
This is...

00:20:17.530 --> 00:20:19.160
The Final Ring.

00:20:19.160 --> 00:20:21.490
With this, you'll be a Phi-Brain too.

00:20:22.870 --> 00:20:24.700
The Final Ring?!

00:20:24.700 --> 00:20:28.620
Sure enough, that's why he stole it from Klondike!

00:20:33.340 --> 00:20:36.340
You and I have earned the right to become gods.

00:20:36.920 --> 00:20:39.880
The Puzzle of God I made is complete.

00:20:40.180 --> 00:20:41.890
No, Kaito!

00:20:41.890 --> 00:20:43.930
Don't be swallowed up by the Ring!

00:20:43.930 --> 00:20:45.760
Who will save Freecell?!

00:20:55.820 --> 00:20:57.770
No!

00:21:15.050 --> 00:21:15.790
Kaito...

00:21:21.050 --> 00:21:25.380
I can fight you without having to borrow its power,

00:21:26.720 --> 00:21:27.890
Freecell!

00:21:32.020 --> 00:21:32.940
Incredible!

00:21:33.580 --> 00:21:36.400
You're so incredible, Kaito!

00:21:42.450 --> 00:21:43.950
Can you see?

00:21:43.950 --> 00:21:46.660
That is the Puzzle of God I've made.

00:21:47.950 --> 00:21:49.160
Shall we go?

00:21:50.120 --> 00:21:51.450
Fine by me.

00:22:01.590 --> 00:22:03.140
They're gone.

00:22:03.140 --> 00:22:04.470
Kaito...

00:22:04.470 --> 00:22:05.800
That bastard!

00:22:05.800 --> 00:22:08.180
By brute force, he refused the Ring!

00:22:08.180 --> 00:22:14.010
Kaito has become someone with
no need of the Orpheus Ring.

00:22:15.020 --> 00:22:19.980
Freecell tried to make
the closed-off world he wanted.

00:22:22.200 --> 00:22:25.490
If they're both of equal strength...

00:22:26.830 --> 00:22:29.240
he'll never be able to return.

00:22:38.710 --> 00:22:40.050
Eiyuukidori
Playing the hero

00:22:40.050 --> 00:22:44.940
Itsudatte shinjita muteki no kankaku
A sense of invincibility you always believed in

00:22:45.550 --> 00:22:51.370
Tatakatte iru no wa chikyuu no tame nanka ja nai
You're not fighting for the sake of the world or anything

00:22:51.370 --> 00:22:54.160
Motto maipeesu de
It's for a more leisurely

00:22:54.160 --> 00:22:59.230
Sou, motto shoujiki na onegai no tame
Yeah, more straightforward request

00:22:59.600 --> 00:23:07.670
Nandotonaku kizutsuitemo tachiagare, hero
Even if you're wounded over and over, rise up, hero

00:23:07.670 --> 00:23:13.220
Kitto daijoubu, kimi o mamorunda
It's sure to be all right, I'll protect you

00:23:13.610 --> 00:23:17.040
Machigai da to shitemo tomarenai
Even if it's wrong, it can't be stopped

00:23:17.040 --> 00:23:20.650
Seikai ka nante wakaranai
I don't know if it's the right answer

00:23:21.550 --> 00:23:24.660
Donna toki demo original ni
No matter the situation

00:23:24.660 --> 00:23:27.400
Step o fumidashiteku
I'll take those first steps, originally

00:23:27.400 --> 00:23:30.770
Dramatic ni, mawaru sekai de
On this spinning world, I'm searching, dramatically

00:23:30.770 --> 00:23:34.430
Kiwameita wonder sagashiteru
For wonders that sparkle

00:23:35.190 --> 00:23:38.430
Boku, shijou saikou no tabi o tsuzukeyou
Me, I'll keep going on the greatest journey in history

00:23:38.430 --> 00:23:42.740
Image shite shiawase na mirai e
To the happy future I imagined

00:23:44.430 --> 00:23:46.060
Mirai e
To the future

00:23:47.920 --> 00:23:51.380
Mirai e
To the future

00:23:51.380 --> 00:23:52.800
Mirai e
To the future

00:23:54.710 --> 00:23:56.260
(Mirai e)
(To the future)

00:24:04.000 --> 00:24:06.800
Kaito, how you sparkle!

00:24:06.800 --> 00:24:09.340
You truly are my aspiration.

00:24:09.340 --> 00:24:12.010
The only one, for as long as I've been alone...

00:24:12.390 --> 00:24:14.560
Come, it's puzzle time,

00:24:15.100 --> 00:24:17.940
using the Puzzle of God I've made!

00:24:18.560 --> 00:24:21.290
Next time, "Release the Infinite Puzzle!"

00:24:21.580 --> 00:24:26.670
Release the Infinite Puzzle!

00:24:22.230 --> 00:24:23.730
Shall we begin?

00:24:23.730 --> 00:24:25.610
Let's play up!
